<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Weld</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal; font-weight:bold;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mesh &gt; Weld</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">or by pressing</span> <span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl + W</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Weld</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command removes surplus triangles. This command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. It works on wholly selected entities as well as on partial selections.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../mesh/Processing_Meshes_files/image122.gif" width="257px" height="165px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Weld vertices closer than</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Maximum distance between vertices that must be welded. Default value for this command is 0.01mm.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP162478961" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="5" class="whs5">
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs6">
<td class="whs7">
<p><img src="../mesh/processing_meshes_files/weld1.gif" width="575px" height="430px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs6">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" class="whs9">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Mesh before Weld applied</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs6">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" class="whs9">
<p><img src="../mesh/processing_meshes_files/weld2.gif" width="575px" height="430px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs6">
<td class="whs9">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Mesh after Weld applied</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">If an area of a mesh is cut away two meshes are formed, the original and the cut section. The vertices around the edges where the two meshes were formerly joined would exist on both meshes. If the cut section is pasted back onto the original mesh, the vertices around the meeting edges would be duplicated.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span class="Command">Weld</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to join the two meshes removing any surplus vertices.</span></p>
